Thanks for the PR @parneetbrar234-svg! 

Logging serialization failures via \console.error\ instead of failing silently is a nice operational improvement, and the new test covering this behavior is solid.

However, in \utils/tracking.ts\, you removed the \username.trim() === ''\ validation check:
\\\	ypescript
-  if (!username || username.trim() === '') {
-    return;
-  }
\\\

While this didn't break any existing tests (because we apparently lacked coverage for it!), removing this check causes a regression where we will now send tracking events with whitespace-only usernames like \{ username: '   ' }\ to the server.

Please restore the \username.trim() === ''\ check. Once that's restored, this will be ready to merge!
